"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<!-- Please search existing issues to avoid creating duplicates -->  \n\n<!-- Please attach logs to help us diagnose your issue -->\n\n* **Copilot Chat Extension Version**:\n* **VS Code Version**:\n* **OS Version**:\n* **Feature** (e.g., agent/edit/ask mode):\n* **Selected model** (e.g., GPT 4.1, Claude 3.7 Sonnet):\n* **Logs**:\n\n**Steps to Reproduce:**\nThis issue occurs frequently. When using Copilot in Agent mode, it often runs the same commands multiple times, even when the commands succeed. It seems that Copilot lacks proper visibility into the command output and doesn’t recognize that the task was completed successfully:\n\n![Screenshot](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ba65f545-d0f8-421d-b3ba-849f2d416fac)\n\nTo work around this, you have to manually copy and paste the output back to Copilot—only then does it realize the command actually succeeded:\n\n![Screenshot](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fd694611-7086-47a0-98ae-93afc4023208)\n\n---\n\nI'm not sure if this issue is specific to WSL2, but I suspect it might be, possibly because Copilot could have troubles reading output from the Bash terminal inside the WSL2 environment.","closed_by":{"login":"bhavyaus","id":25044782,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MDQ0Nzgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25044782?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus","html_url":"https://github.com/bhavyaus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/subscripti